##### Q1 (v4, local gpt-oss:20b, 1 run): In the 2024 Bahrain Grand Prix, who had the faster race pace, Verstappen or Norris? Use only green-flag laps, excluding in-laps, out-laps and deleted laps. Give the median lap time for each.
== run 1 ==
  step 1 SQL: SELECT Abbreviation, median(LapTime)/1e9 AS median_sec FROM laps WHERE race='bahrain_grand_prix' AND session='R' AND TrackStatus='1' AND PitInTime IS NULL AND PitOutTime IS NULL AND Deleted IS NOT TRUE AND Abbreviation IN ('VER','NOR') GROUP BY Abbreviation;
  step 2 SQL: SELECT Driver, median(LapTime)/1e9 AS median_sec FROM laps WHERE race='bahrain_grand_prix' AND session='R' AND TrackStatus='1' AND PitInTime IS NULL AND PitOutTime IS NULL AND Deleted IS NOT TRUE AND LapTime IS NOT NULL AND Driver IN ('VER','NOR') GROUP BY Driver;
  step 3 SQL: SELECT ds.full_name, median(l.LapTime)/1e9 AS median_sec FROM laps l JOIN driver_seasons ds ON l.Driver = ds.driver_code AND l.season = ds.season WHERE l.race='bahrain_grand_prix' AND l.session='R' AND l.TrackStatus='1' AND l.PitInTime IS NULL AND l.PitOutTime IS NULL AND l.Deleted IS NOT TRUE AND l.LapTime IS NOT NULL AND l.Driver IN ('VER','NOR') GROUP BY ds.full_name;
steps=3 ANSWER: 'In the 2024 Bahrain Grand Prix, **Max\u202fVerstappen** had the faster race pace.\n\n| Driver | Median green‑flag lap time (seconds) |\n|--------|-------------------------------------|\n| Max\u202fVerstappen | **95.48\u202fs** |\n| Lando\u202fNorris | **96.54\u202fs** |\n\nVerstappen’s median lap was about 1.06\u202fs quicker than Norris’s.'
##### Q2 (v4, local gpt-oss:20b, 1 run): Across the 2024 Grand Prix races, which drivers finished on the podium (top 3) after starting outside the top 10 on the grid? Give each driver with how many times they did it.
== run 1 ==
  step 1 SQL: SELECT ds.full_name, COUNT(*) as podiums
FROM results r
JOIN driver_seasons ds ON r.Abbreviation = ds.driver_code AND r.season = ds.season
WHERE r.session='R' AND r.Position <=3 AND r.GridPosition >10
GROUP BY ds.full_name
ORDER BY podiums DESC;
  step 2 SQL: SELECT r.Abbreviation, ds.full_name, r.GridPosition, r.Position, r.race
FROM results r
JOIN driver_seasons ds ON r.Abbreviation = ds.driver_code AND r.season = ds.season
WHERE r.session='R' AND r.Position <=3 AND r.GridPosition >10
ORDER BY r.race;
  step 3 SQL: SELECT r.Abbreviation, ds.full_name, r.GridPosition, r.Position, r.race
FROM results r
JOIN driver_seasons ds ON r.Abbreviation = ds.driver_code AND r.season = ds.season
WHERE r.session='R' AND r.Position <=3 AND r.GridPosition >10
ORDER BY r.race;
steps=3 ANSWER: '**Drivers who reached the podium after starting outside the top‑10 (2024 season)**  \n\n| Driver | Podium finishes |\n|--------|-----------------|\n| Max\u202fVerstappen | 1 |\n| Pierre\u202fGasly | 1 |\n| Charles\u202fLeclerc | 1 |\n\nEach of these drivers achieved a podium position (1st‑3rd) in a race where their grid start was 11th or lower.'
##### Q3 (v4, local gpt-oss:20b, 1 run): Across the 2024 season, which driver had the largest gap between their best qualifying lap and their median race lap at the same Grand Prix? Use green-flag race laps only (excluding in-laps, out-laps and deleted laps) for the race median, and ignore deleted qualifying laps. Give the driver, the Grand Prix, and the gap in seconds.
== run 1 ==
  step 1 SQL: WITH best_q AS (
  SELECT race, Abbreviation as driver, MIN(LapTime) as best_q
  FROM laps
  WHERE session='Q' AND LapTime IS NOT NULL AND Deleted IS NOT TRUE
  GROUP BY race, Abbreviation
),
median_r AS (
  SELECT race, Abbreviation as driver,
    percentile_cont(0.5) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY LapTime) AS median_r
  FROM laps
  WHERE session='R' AND LapTime IS NOT NULL AND Deleted IS NOT TRUE
    AND TrackStatus='1' AND PitInTime IS NULL AND PitOutTime IS NULL
  GROUP BY race, Abbreviation
)
SELECT ds.full_name, br.race, (median_r - best_q)/1e9 AS gap_seconds
FROM median_r
JOIN best_q ON median_r.race=best_q.race AND median_r.driver=best_q.driver
JOIN driver_seasons ds ON ds.driver_code=median_r.driver AND ds.season=2024
ORDER BY gap_seconds DESC
LIMIT 1;
  step 2 SQL: WITH best_q AS (
  SELECT race, Driver as driver, MIN(LapTime) as best_q
  FROM laps
  WHERE session='Q' AND LapTime IS NOT NULL AND Deleted IS NOT TRUE
  GROUP BY race, Driver
),
median_r AS (
  SELECT race, Driver as driver,
    percentile_cont(0.5) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY LapTime) AS median_r
  FROM laps
  WHERE session='R' AND LapTime IS NOT NULL AND Deleted IS NOT TRUE
    AND TrackStatus='1' AND PitInTime IS NULL AND PitOutTime IS NULL
  GROUP BY race, Driver
)
SELECT ds.full_name, br.race, (median_r - best_q)/1e9 AS gap_seconds
FROM median_r
JOIN best_q ON median_r.race=best_q.race AND median_r.driver=best_q.driver
JOIN driver_seasons ds ON ds.driver_code=median_r.driver AND ds.season=2024
ORDER BY gap_seconds DESC
LIMIT 1;
  step 3 SQL: WITH best_q AS (
  SELECT race, Driver as driver, MIN(LapTime) as best_q
  FROM laps
  WHERE session='Q' AND LapTime IS NOT NULL AND Deleted IS NOT TRUE
  GROUP BY race, Driver
),
median_r AS (
  SELECT race, Driver as driver,
    percentile_cont(0.5) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY LapTime) AS median_r
  FROM laps
  WHERE session='R' AND LapTime IS NOT NULL AND Deleted IS NOT TRUE
    AND TrackStatus='1' AND PitInTime IS NULL AND PitOutTime IS NULL
  GROUP BY race, Driver
)
SELECT ds.full_name, best_q.race, (median_r - best_q)/1e9 AS gap_seconds
FROM median_r
JOIN best_q ON median_r.race=best_q.race AND median_r.driver=best_q.driver
JOIN driver_seasons ds ON ds.driver_code=median_r.driver AND ds.season=2024
ORDER BY gap_seconds DESC
LIMIT 1;
steps=3 ANSWER: 'Logan\u202fSargeant – Canadian Grand Prix – 16.767\u202fseconds.'
##### Q4 (v4, local gpt-oss:20b, 1 run): Across all 2024 Grand Prix races, how many laps did each driver lead? Count a lap as led when the driver's Position is 1 on that lap. Give the driver with the most laps led and their count.
== run 1 ==
  step 1 SQL: SELECT l.Driver, COUNT(*) AS laps_led
FROM laps l
WHERE l.session = 'R' AND l.Position = 1
GROUP BY l.Driver
ORDER BY laps_led DESC
LIMIT 50;
  step 2 SQL: SELECT ds.full_name, l.Driver, COUNT(*) AS laps_led
FROM laps l
JOIN driver_seasons ds ON ds.driver_code = l.Driver AND ds.season = 2024
WHERE l.session = 'R' AND l.Position = 1
GROUP BY ds.full_name, l.Driver
ORDER BY laps_led DESC;
steps=2 ANSWER: '**Laps led by each driver in the 2024 season**\n\n| Driver | Laps led |\n|--------|----------|\n| Max\u202fVerstappen | 559 |\n| Lando\u202fNorris | 271 |\n| Charles\u202fLeclerc | 172 |\n| George\u202fRussell | 137 |\n| Carlos\u202fSainz | 134 |\n| Oscar\u202fPiastri | 123 |\n| Lewis\u202fHamilton | 31 |\n| Esteban\u202fOcon | 14 |\n| Sergio\u202fPerez | 1 |\n\n**Driver with the most laps led**\n\n- **Max\u202fVerstappen – 559 laps led**'
